OCPROJECT 1
# Engine test content for visual scripting. NOT a demo project and not a game -- it exists so the
# graph vocabulary can be proven against a real running executable without reaching into anyone's
# irreplaceable project, and so the sample graph under Content/Scripts is provably free of any
# project's assumptions.
#
# WHAT IT PROVES. AverGame's project-graph auto-discovery ticks every .ocgraph under a project's
# Content against its own entity. IdleMotion.ocgraph seeds itself from whatever entity it is handed
# and writes that entity's position directly, so running this project is the end-to-end evidence
# that a single graph file can drive an entity with no host code, no position sink and no OUT
# convention -- the thing that previously required bespoke per-entity C# in every project that
# wanted more than one of something.
NAME GraphDemo
ENGINE Aver 0.1.2
CREATEDWITH 0.2.0
CONTENT Content
# STARTMAP: GRAPH-AS-CLASS needs a real placed entity to prove itself against (a graph cannot drive
# an entity that does not exist), so Maps/OrbitDemo.ocmap places two AN_Orbiter instances -- see
# that file's own header for what it proves. IdleMotion.ocgraph itself is unchanged in spirit: still
# the same self-seeding, host-code-free graph the auto-discovery path already ran; it just now ALSO
# carries a CLASS record, so it is discovered twice over -- once as the class OrbitDemo.ocmap's
# placements instantiate, and (for any OTHER .ocgraph a future addition drops in this project with no
# CLASS record) still via the original synthetic-entity auto-discovery, unaffected.
STARTMAP Maps/OrbitDemo.ocmap
